    <sys:String x:Key="Btn_Plus">＋</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_AddABlankLayerAbove">Add a blank layer above the current one (Ctrl+Shift+N). The first time, the existing content becomes "Layer 1".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DuplicateTheCurrentLayerWith">Duplicate the current layer (with every frame's content), placing it directly above</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DeleteTheCurrentLayerAt">Delete the current layer (at least one must remain; Ctrl+Z undoes it)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MoveTheCurrentLayerUp">Move the current layer up one (it covers more)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MoveTheCurrentLayerDown">Move the current layer down one</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MergeDownLayTheCurrent">Merge down: lay the current layer onto the one below, making the two one layer (all frames)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_LayerListUpperLayersCover">Layer list (upper layers cover lower ones). Click a row = edit that layer; the tick on the left = show / hide; double-click = rename. The pencil, fill, selection, image import and inflate all act on the current layer.</sys:String>
