    <sys:String x:Key="Hdr_Tools">Tools</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Pencil">Pencil</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Eraser">Eraser</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Select">Select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DragOutASelectionBox">Drag out a selection box (thickness = brush depth). Ctrl+C copy, Ctrl+X cut, Ctrl+V paste, Delete delete; drag inside the box to move it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PressToSetTheStart">Press to set the start, drag to the end and release. Draws with the current brush (shape / size / depth / 3D brush); left button draws the current colour, right button erases. Hold Shift to constrain to horizontal / vertical / 45°. Esc cancels. Shortcut L.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DragOutTheCornersOf">Drag out the corners of a rectangle and release; by default only the outline is drawn, tick "Fill shape" for solid. Hold Shift for a square. Left draws, right erases. Esc cancels. Shortcut R.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DragOutTheBoundingRectangle">Drag out the bounding rectangle of an ellipse and release; by default only the outline is drawn, tick "Fill shape" for solid. Hold Shift for a circle. Left draws, right erases. Esc cancels. Shortcut E.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ClickAVoxelOnThe">Click a voxel on the canvas to make its colour the brush colour (clicking an empty cell picks the transparent colour). Hold and drag to keep picking. Shortcut I.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ClickToSelectTheConnected">Click to select the "connected region of the same colour" in the current slice (clicking empty space selects the connected empty area). Shift+click = add to the selection, Ctrl+click = subtract. Thickness = brush depth. Once selected you can copy, cut, delete, or drag the selection to move it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ClickAVoxelToSelect">Click a voxel to select the whole part that is connected to it in 3D (by default all connected coloured voxels; can be changed to same colour only). Then move it as a block with the arrow keys or the buttons below, or move it to a new layer and assemble it elsewhere. Shift+click = add, Ctrl+click = subtract.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_LeftButtonDrawsFillsRight">Left button draws / fills, right button erases / clears the region</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_3DMagicWandParts">3D magic wand (parts)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_SameColourOnly">Same colour only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_TickedOnlyVoxelsOfThe">Ticked: only voxels of the same colour that are connected to the clicked one; unticked: all connected coloured voxels (any colour)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_DiagonalsCountAsConnected26">Diagonals count as connected (26-connected)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ByDefaultOnlyNeighboursSharing">By default only neighbours sharing a face count (6-connected); when ticked, diagonal neighbours sharing an edge or corner also count as connected</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveLeft">Move the whole block one cell left (arrow key ←)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveRight">Move the whole block one cell right (arrow key →)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveUp">Move the whole block one cell up (arrow key ↑)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveDown">Move the whole block one cell down (arrow key ↓)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveForward">Move the whole block one slice toward the viewer (Ctrl+↑); the slice slider follows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Btn_Forward">Forward</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PartMoveBack">Move the whole block one slice away from the viewer (Ctrl+↓)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Btn_Back">Back</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_CutTheSelectedPartOut">Cut the selected part out of the current layer and put it in a new layer above it (the selection follows). When it is assembled, use "Merge down" to combine it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Btn_MoveToNewLayer">Move to new layer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Btn_DeleteSelection">Delete selection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_DeleteTheSelectedVoxelsDelete">Delete the selected voxels (Delete)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_FillShapesRectangleEllipse">Fill shapes (rectangle / ellipse)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ForTheRectangleAndEllipse">For the rectangle and ellipse tools: ticked = draw solid, unticked = outline only.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_3DFill">3D fill</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_TickedReplacesTheConnectedSolid">Ticked: replaces the connected solid block of the same colour in the whole volume (clicking an empty cell does nothing). Unticked: fills only the connected same-colour region in the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_GlobalSameColour">Global same colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ForTheMagicWandTicked">For the magic wand: ticked = select ALL cells of the same colour in the current slice (connection not required). Unticked = only the same-colour region connected to the clicked cell.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_MagicWandTolerance">Magic wand tolerance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_WandTolerance">For the magic wand: 0 = only exactly the same colour. The larger the number, the more similar colours are also selected (each of R, G, B and A differs from the clicked colour by no more than this number). Transparent cells only count as the same as transparent cells.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_MagicWandFeatherCells">Magic wand feather (cells)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_WandFeather">For the magic wand: 0 = hard edge. N = the selection edge fades "inward" over N cells (the outermost ring is only slightly selected, more toward the inside). When deleting, the edge is only partly faded; when copying / cutting / moving / pasting, the edge is blended into the colours underneath as semi-transparent (this uses free palette slots). It is decided at the moment of selection; moving the slider later does not affect an already-made selection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Hdr_Brush">Brush</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MirrorsAroundTheExactCentre">Mirrors around the exact centre of the model (using the model's X / Y / Z axes, the same in every view). When on, every cell changed by the pencil, eraser (including 3D brushes) and fill is also set to the same value at the mirrored position; several axes can be on at once. Selection and paste are not affected. The pink dashed lines on the canvas are the mirror axes lying in this view's plane, and the pink box is the cursor at the mirrored position.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MirrorOnXLeftRight">Mirror on X (left-right symmetric along the length)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MirrorOnYFrontBack">Mirror on Y (front-back symmetric along the width)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_MirrorOnZUpDown">Mirror on Z (up-down symmetric along the height)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_Shape">Shape</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Square">Square</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_FlatSquareSizeSideLength">Flat square, size = side length. Use "Depth" to stack more slices behind.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Circle">Circle</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_FlatCircleSizeDiameterUse">Flat circle, size = diameter. Use "Depth" to stack more slices behind.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Cube">Cube</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushCentredOn">3D brush: centred on the clicked cell and the current slice; size = side length (this many cells left-right, up-down and front-back). Depth is not used. Anything outside the model is cropped automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Ellipsoid">Ellipsoid</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushSizeThe">3D brush: size = the radius on the canvas (left-right, up-down), total length along the line of sight = brush depth. Depth = 2×radius+1 gives a ball; shorter is flattened, longer is a stretched rugby-ball shape. Centred on the clicked cell and the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Spring">Spring</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushTheSame">3D brush: the same helix as "Helix", but the wire is thick (3 cells), so it turns once every "radius+6" slices and the coils do not stick together. Size = spring radius, axis along the line of sight, total length = brush depth.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Helix">Helix</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushOneContinuous">3D brush: one continuous helix 1 voxel thick. Size = helix radius, axis along the line of sight (through the clicked cell), total length = brush depth, one turn every "radius+4" slices. It starts at the right side of the rearmost slice and turns clockwise on the canvas toward the front.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Torus">Torus</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushDonutSize">3D brush (donut): size = ring radius (the clicked cell is the hole in the middle); the tube thickness (tube diameter) = brush depth, i.e. how many slices thick along the line of sight. The ring lies flat on the canvas; depth 1 = one flat ring. Centred on the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Pyramid">Pyramid</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushSizeSide">3D brush: size = side length of the square base, axis along the line of sight (perpendicular to the canvas), length = brush depth. The base is at the back (largest side) and the tip points toward you (shrinking slice by slice). Centred on the clicked cell and the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Cone">Cone</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_3DBrushSizeBase">3D brush: size = base radius, axis along the line of sight (perpendicular to the canvas), length = brush depth. The base is at the back (largest radius) and the tip points toward you (shrinking slice by slice). Centred on the clicked cell and the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Cylinder">Cylinder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_BrushCylinder">3D brush: size = radius, axis along the line of sight (perpendicular to the canvas), length = brush depth; every slice is the same disc and both ends are flat. Centred on the clicked cell and the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_Capsule">Capsule</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_BrushCapsule">3D brush: size = radius, axis along the line of sight (perpendicular to the canvas), total axial length = brush depth (including the two hemispheres; if the depth is shorter than the ball's diameter it is just a ball). Centred on the clicked cell and the current slice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_SizeSideLength">Size (side length)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_Depth">Depth</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_1DrawOnlyTheCurrent">1 = draw only the current slice. 2 or more = draw the current slice and also that many slices behind it along the line of sight (away from you, slice numbers getting smaller). Works with the pencil, eraser and (flat) fill; 3D fill already spans slices and does not use depth.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_DrawOnlyTheCurrentSlice">Draw only the current slice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Hdr_Display">Display</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_ShowNextSliceSemiTransparent">Show next slice semi-transparent</sys:String>
