    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SelectionAndEditing">Selection and editing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_MagicWand">Magic wand</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SelectsTheConnectedRegionOf">Selects the connected region of the same colour; Shift adds, Ctrl subtracts; you can tick "Global same colour" and set "Tolerance" and "Feather".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CutCopyPasteDeleteSelect">Cut, copy, paste, delete, select all</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlXCVDelete">Ctrl+X / C / V, Delete, Ctrl+A; after pasting you can drag it to the place you want before dropping it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AnyAngleEditMenuOr">Any angle (Edit menu, or Ctrl+] / Ctrl+[ for 15° each); the result is still floating, so you can rotate or drag it again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CopyTo1SliceCtrl">Copy to +1 slice (Ctrl+D), −1 slice (Ctrl+Shift+D), or to a whole range at once; you can tick "Don't overwrite transparent".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_DuplicateSlice">Duplicate slice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ClearsTheWholeSliceSeen">Clears the whole slice seen in the current view.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_ClearThisSlice">Clear this slice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FlipHorizontallyFlipVertically">Flip horizontally, flip vertically, rotate 90° / 180°, shift (Edit menu).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WholeSliceWholeFrameTransforms">Whole-slice / whole-frame transforms</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlZUpTo200">Ctrl+Z, up to 200 steps; strokes, selection moves, slice copies, adding or removing frames and palette tidying can all be undone.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_Undo">Undo</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_RGBAColourPicking">RGBA colour picking</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PickWithTheSquareAnd">Pick with the square and two sliders (including opacity), or type 0–255 directly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ColourAndPalette">Colour and palette</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AnotherWayToPickHue">Another way to pick: hue, saturation and value.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_HSVTab">HSV tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SharedPalette">Shared palette</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_UpTo255ColoursShared">Up to 255 colours, shared by all frames; a colour is only recorded in the palette once you paint with it; the transparent colour is always in the first slot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ToolsMenuPaletteRemovesColours">Tools menu &gt; Palette: removes colours that no frame uses, freeing slots.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_RemoveUnusedColours">Remove unused colours</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_MergeDuplicateColours">Merge duplicate colours</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ToolsMenuPaletteIdenticalColours">Tools menu &gt; Palette: identical colours keep only one slot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ImportExportPalette">Import / export palette</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_GIMPPaletteGpl">GIMP palette (.gpl).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayersAndPartAssembly">Layers and part assembly</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ToTheLeftOfThe">To the left of the timeline is the layer list: shared by the whole animation, with one cel per layer in every frame. Upper layers cover lower ones. The pencil, fill, selection, image import and inflate all act on the current layer; the preview, timeline thumbnails, playback and exports show the composited result.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MultipleLayers">Multiple layers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_NewCtrlShiftNAbove">New (Ctrl+Shift+N, above the current layer), duplicate, delete, move up / down, merge down, flatten all layers; click a row to switch the current layer, the tick on the left = show / hide, double-click to rename. Every action is one undo step (even the layer content comes back).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayerCommands">Layer commands</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_BackgroundReference">Background reference</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WithSeveralLayersTheEdit">With several layers, the edit canvas draws the content of the other layers semi-transparent underneath the transparent parts of the current layer, to help with alignment.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Common_ImportFileAsLayer">Import file as layer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayerMenuReadsAnotherPstk">Layer menu: reads another .pstk (a component) and puts it above the current layer as a new layer. If the sizes differ it is centred; colours are mapped to the current palette; a component with a single frame is put in every frame.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayerMenuShiftsAllVoxels">Layer menu: shifts all voxels of the current layer by X / Y / Z cells as one block (this frame only, or this layer's content in every frame); anything moved outside the model is dropped, and it can be undone.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Tool3DMagicWand">Tool "3D magic wand": click a voxel to select the whole part connected to it in 3D (can be changed to same colour only, and can include diagonal connections); Shift adds, Ctrl subtracts. The selected part is tinted yellow on the canvas.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_3DMagicWand">3D magic wand</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AfterSelectingAPartMove">After selecting a part, move it as a block with the arrow keys (Ctrl+↑ / ↓ for forward / back) or the panel buttons; Delete deletes it; "Move to new layer" cuts it into a new layer above, and merging down puts it together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MoveAndExtractParts">Move and extract parts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AnimationFrameByFrame">Animation (frame by frame)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MultiFrameTimeline">Multi-frame timeline</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AtTheBottomIsA">At the bottom is a thumbnail of every frame; click one to switch to it and edit.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AddBlankFrameDuplicateFrame">Add blank frame, duplicate frame, delete frame, move left, move right.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FrameManagement">Frame management</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PlaybackAndSpeed">Playback and speed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SpacePlaysPausesSpeed1">Space plays / pauses; speed 1–30 frames per second.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PressAndForThePrevious">Press , and . for the previous and next frame.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ChangeFrame">Change frame</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ShownLiveOnTheRight">Shown live on the right; drag to rotate and change the pitch, the wheel zooms in and out, double-click resets.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LivePseudo3DPreview">Live pseudo-3D preview</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_3DPreview">3D preview</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SolidVoxelsShowsWhatYou">Solid voxels (shows what you see) and stacked (Sprite Stacking style).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TwoPreviewModes">Two preview modes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AutoRotateCanBeSwitched">Auto-rotate can be switched on and off; shading can be turned off to see flat colours.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AutoRotateAndShading">Auto-rotate and shading</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ShowsOnlyThePartBehind">Shows only the part behind the current slice, to check the inside.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CutOpenToSeeInside">Cut open to see inside</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CollapsibleFunctionBars">Collapsible function bars</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheLeftColumnIsSplit">The left column is split into five categories — view, colour, tools, brush and display — which can be collapsed or expanded, and the state is remembered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Interface">Interface</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheTimelineAndTheSlice">The timeline and the layer slider + copy tools each have a title bar; click it to collapse and give the edit canvas and preview more room. While collapsed, Space, , . , ←/→ and [ ] still work, and the state is remembered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CollapsibleTimelineAndSlicePanels">Collapsible timeline and slice panels</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WheelZones">Wheel zones</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MouseOverTheLeftColumn">Mouse over the left column = scroll the function bars, middle = change slice, right = zoom the 3D preview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MouseTips">Mouse tips</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AlmostEveryButtonAndOption">Almost every button and option shows an explanation if you hold the mouse over it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheUserGuideInThe">The "User guide…" in the Help menu (F1): this very document.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PixelStackingIsAnEditorFor">PixelStacking is an editor for "voxel" models and animation: a model is a stack of flat slices; you edit one slice from any direction and see the 3D result live on the right.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_OverviewIntro">There are {0} features in {1} categories. The tabs on the left hold the quick start, recommended workflows, shortcuts and FAQ.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CategoryTitle">{0} ({1} items)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FeatureLine">{0}: {1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_QuickStart">Quick start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MakeYourFirstModelIn">Make your first model in about five minutes:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PressCtrlNForA">Press Ctrl+N for a new document. For the first time 32 × 32 × 32 (length × width × height, 1–128 each) is a good size; more cells means more detail but slower drawing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PickAColourInThe">Pick a colour: in the left column "Colour", adjust RGBA with the square and sliders, or click a swatch below. A colour is only recorded in the palette once you paint with it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_StartDrawingTheDefaultView">Start drawing: the default view is "Top", and the canvas shows one slice of the model. Choose "Pencil" and paint with the left button, erase with the right.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ChangeSliceScrollTheWheel">Change layer: press ← and →, or [ and ]. A higher number is closer to you. Draw a little on each layer and the model grows taller.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PaintIn3DWith">Paint in 3D with one stroke: in the left column "Brush" pick "Ellipsoid", "Cube", "Cylinder"…, one click is a whole blob; or raise "Depth" to paint several slices behind at once.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SeeTheResultThe3">See the result: the 3D preview on the right updates live. Drag to rotate, wheel to zoom, double-click to reset.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AddDetailFromAnotherAngle">Add detail from another angle: press 1–6 (top, bottom, front, back, left, right) to edit from another direction; feet are easier to see from the front and the back from the side, which makes alignment easier.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SaveCtrlSSavesAs">Save: Ctrl+S saves as .pstk. A "*" means it is not saved yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ForGamesFileExportPNG">For games: File → Export PNG (pre-rendered pictures), Export GIF (to share), Export stack strip (so the game stacks it itself).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WhenYouCanTFind">When you can't find a feature, hold the mouse over it for a few seconds; almost every control has an explanation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_DrawingAndSelectionTips">Drawing and selection tips</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_DrawFaster">Draw faster</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LeftRightSymmetricCharactersIn">Left-right symmetric characters: in the left column "Brush" tick X under "Mirror symmetry" and draw only half. For front-back or up-down symmetry tick Y or Z; several can be on together. The pink dashed lines on the canvas are the mirror axes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LargeAreasUseFillTick">Large areas: use "Fill". Tick "3D fill" to replace a whole connected solid block of the same colour at once (clicking an empty cell does nothing).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CirclesBoxesLinesUseLine">Circles, boxes, lines: use "Line", "Rectangle" and "Ellipse", which show a preview while you drag; Shift gives a circle, a square or a 45° line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AWholeWallOrA">A whole wall or a whole pillar: draw one slice and use "Copy to range…", or press Ctrl+D repeatedly to stack upward.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_3DBrushesEllipsoidFor">3D brushes: ellipsoid for heads (depth = 2×radius+1 gives a true sphere), capsule for arms and legs, torus for donuts or tyres, helix and spring for coils. Depth decides the length along the line of sight.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SelectingAndModifying">Selecting and modifying</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SelectDragsOutARectangle">"Select" drags out a rectangle; "Magic wand" selects the connected region of the same colour with one click (Shift adds, Ctrl subtracts). Thickness = brush depth, so a large depth selects several slices at once.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheMagicWandSTolerance">The magic wand's "Tolerance" lets similar colours be selected together; "Feather" fades the edge (inward only).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AfterSelectingYouCanCtrl">After selecting you can Ctrl+C / X / V, or drag inside the box to move it; while the content is floating (being moved or just pasted) the arrow keys nudge it by 1 cell. Enter drops it, Esc cancels.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_RotateSelectionEditMenuOr">"Rotate selection" (Edit menu, or Ctrl+] / Ctrl+[) turns it by any angle, along the line of sight around the centre of the selection. To rotate around another axis, switch to that view and rotate there.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TransformAllSlicesOfThe">"Transform all slices of the current layer" flips, rotates 90° or shifts the whole current layer, as if the whole layer moved together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WhenPastingTickDonT">When pasting, tick "Don't overwrite transparent" so only cells with colour are pasted and what was underneath is not cleared.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_DisplayAids">Display aids</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ShowNextSliceSemiTransparent">"Show next slice semi-transparent" shows what the slice behind looks like, for alignment. "Show previous frame semi-transparent" (orange) is very useful when animating.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TickCutOpenToSee">Tick "Cut open to see inside" in the preview on the right to show only the part behind the current slice and check whether the inside is drawn correctly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ADocumentCanHaveMany">A document can have many frames, and all frames share the same palette and size. The most direct way is to draw frame by frame:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FinishTheFirstFramePress">Finish the first frame. Press "Duplicate frame"; the new frame is added after it and selected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FineTuneTheNewFrame">Fine-tune the new frame (raise the hand a bit, move a foot). "Show previous frame semi-transparent" marks the previous frame in orange, which makes alignment easy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Repeat1And2On">Repeat 1 and 2. On the timeline at the bottom you can click thumbnails to switch, "◀ Move left" / "Move right ▶" to change the order, and "Delete frame" to remove ones you don't want.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PressSpaceOrPlayTo">Press Space or "Play" to watch the animation, and set the speed with the slider (1–30 frames per second). , and . switch to the previous and next frame.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FileExportGIFToShare">File → Export GIF to share, or export PNG / stack strip for games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MultipleLayersLetYouSplit">Multiple layers let you split a character into several objects (body, hat, weapon…), draw and move them separately, then merge them into one. To the left of the timeline is the layer list:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_UpperLayersCoverLowerOnes">Upper layers cover lower ones; every layer has its own content in every frame. With just one layer it works exactly as before.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheCanvasEditsTheCurrent">The canvas edits the "current layer" (the row with the blue frame in the list); other layers are shown semi-transparent underneath as a reference. The preview, thumbnails and exports show the composited result.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_NewAboveTheCurrentLayer">＋ New (above the current layer), ⧉ duplicate, ✕ delete, ▲▼ change order, ⤓ merge down; the tick on the left = show / hide; double-click to rename. The Layer menu also has "Flatten all layers".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ImportAComponentAndAssemble">Import a component and assemble it onto the character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayerMenuImportFileAs">Layer menu → Import file as layer…, and pick another .pstk (for example a hat). It becomes a new layer above the current one, centred if the sizes differ.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LayerMenuMoveLayerContent">Layer menu → Move layer content…, and enter X / Y / Z cells to move the whole component into place (this frame only, or all frames together).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WhenItLooksRightPress">When it looks right, press ⤓ merge down and the component is merged into the body layer. To undo it, press Ctrl+Z.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_UseThe3DMagic">Use the 3D magic wand to take a part out of the model</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_InTheLeftColumnChoose">In the left column choose the "3D magic wand" tool and click a voxel on the model. The whole block connected to it in 3D is selected (tinted yellow). "Same colour only" and "Diagonals count as connected" adjust the range.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_MoveItWithTheArrow">Move it with the arrow keys ← → ↑ ↓, and Ctrl+↑ / ↓ for forward / back (in the direction of the current view). To change the view press 1–6, then keep moving.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PressMoveToNewLayer">Press "Move to new layer"; the block is cut into a new layer and the selection follows it, so you can keep moving it; when it is in place use "Merge down" to put it back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ImportedComponentsAndExtracted">Imported components and extracted parts live in "their own layer"; if you move one wrongly, press Ctrl+Z at any time, or delete that layer and start over, and the original character is never damaged.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_RecommendedWorkflow">Recommended workflow</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Size">Size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_StartSmall1632To">Start small (16–32) to get the shape right, then scale up once decided. The larger the size, the slower every preview, and the bigger the file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheSizeIsDecidedWhen">The size is decided when you create the document and cannot be changed later, so settle the design at a small size first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_DrawingOrder">Drawing order</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_DecideThePaletteBeforeDrawing">Decide the palette before drawing. There are at most 255 slots; when done you can tidy up with "Palette → Remove unused colours / Merge duplicate colours".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_SavingAndSafety">Saving and safety</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_PressCtrlSOftenBefore">Press Ctrl+S often. Before a big change use "Save as" to keep a copy. Undo goes back up to 200 steps and is gone when you close the program.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_OutputForGames">Output for games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_IfTheGameOnlyNeeds">If the game only needs to "show a rotating 3D character": use "Export PNG", choose how many angles you want, and you get an atlas (or PNG sequence) + JSON.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_IfTheGameWantsTo">If the game wants to stack and rotate the slices itself (Sprite Stacking): use "Export stack strip".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_JustSharingAnAnimationExport">Just sharing an animation: "Export GIF".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ShortcutsAndMouse">Shortcuts and mouse</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FileAndEdit">File and edit</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlNNewCtrlO">Ctrl+N new, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+Shift+S save as, Ctrl+I import image.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlZUndoCtrlX">Ctrl+Z undo. Ctrl+X cut, Ctrl+C copy, Ctrl+V paste, Ctrl+A select all, Delete deletes the selection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlDCopyToSlice">Ctrl+D copy to slice +1, Ctrl+Shift+D copy to slice −1.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CtrlRotatesTheSelection15">Ctrl+] rotates the selection 15° clockwise, Ctrl+[ 15° counter-clockwise.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_EnterDropsFloatingContentEsc">Enter drops floating content, Esc cancels the selection or shape, the arrow keys nudge floating content by 1 cell.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ToolsAndViews">Tools and views</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_IEyedropperLLineR">I eyedropper, L line, R rectangle, E ellipse. Other tools are chosen by clicking in the left column.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_1Top2Bottom3">1 top, 2 bottom, 3 front, 4 back, 5 left, 6 right.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AndPageDownAndPageUpChange">← and →, [ and ], PageDown and PageUp: change layer (with a floating selection or a 3D wand selection, ←/→ move the selection instead).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_AndPreviousAndNextFrame">, and .: previous and next frame. Space: play / pause. F1: open this guide.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Mouse">Mouse</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CanvasLeftButtonPaintsOr">Canvas: left button paints (or applies the current tool), right button erases / clears.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheWheelDependsOnWhere">The wheel depends on where the cursor is: left column = scroll the tool list; over the canvas = scroll up/down (Shift + wheel scrolls sideways, Ctrl + wheel zooms); over the layer and copy tools panel = change layer; right preview column = zoom the 3D preview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_3DPreviewDragTo">3D preview: drag to rotate and change the pitch, wheel to zoom, double-click to reset.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LineRectangleEllipseHoldShift">Line / rectangle / ellipse: hold Shift while dragging to constrain the shape; magic wand and select: Shift adds, Ctrl subtracts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FAQ">FAQ</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Drawing">Drawing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CanTSeeWhatYou">Can't see what you drew? Check that the current "slice" is the one you meant to paint (the number above the canvas); it could also be that the colour is too transparent (the A bar).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_OneStrokePaintsSeveralSlices">One stroke paints several slices? That's "Depth" above 1, or a 3D brush is chosen. To paint only one slice set depth back to 1 and choose a square or circle shape.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheWheelIsnTDoing">The wheel isn't doing what you want? It depends on the cursor: left column scrolls the tool list, the canvas scrolls up/down (Shift sideways, Ctrl zoom), the layer panel changes layer, the right side zooms the preview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_Files">Files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ImportedColoursReducedOrTurned">Imported colours reduced or turned into similar ones? The palette has at most 255 colours; when there aren't enough free slots new colours are quantized; use "Remove unused colours" first to make room.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_OpeningOldFilesEveryOld">Opening old files? Every old-version .pstk can be opened; files saved by a newer version (with a rig) cannot be opened by the older program.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_KeepsAskingWhetherToSave">Keeps asking whether to save when closing? A "*" after the file name in the status bar means there are unsaved changes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_CopyPromptForAI">Copy "prompt for AI"</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_LetAnAISuchAs">Let an AI such as Claude build models with the command-line pstk.exe: paste this text to the AI and it will read the manual first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Menu_OpenAIManual">Open AI manual…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_TheManualForAIsAI">The manual for AIs (AI說明書.md): every command of the command-line pstk.exe and the recommended workflow.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Ai_PstkMissing">Cannot find the command-line pstk.exe: {0}&#10;Please rebuild the project (building the editor also builds pstk.exe).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Main_PromptForAI">Prompt for AI</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Main_CopiedThePromptForAI">Copied the "prompt for AI". Paste it to Claude or another AI and replace the last line with what you want done; it will read the manual first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Main_TheClipboardIsTemporarilyUnavailable">The clipboard is temporarily unavailable. Please try again in a moment.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Ai_ManualMissing">Cannot find the manual: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Main_AIManual">AI manual</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_FourLanguages">Four languages</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheToolsLanguageMenuSwitches">The "Tools &gt; 語言 / Language" menu switches between 繁體中文, English, 日本語 and 한국어; it takes effect at once and is remembered; the first launch follows the operating-system language.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ForAI">For AI</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_HelpMenuCopyPromptFor">Help menu "Copy prompt for AI" plus the command-line pstk.exe (no window; drawing voxels, importing images, inflate, layers, magic wand, rig and preset library and export can all be commanded); the prompt tells the AI to read the manual (AI說明書.md) before doing anything.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_LanguageAndAI">Language and AI</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_ChangeTheInterfaceLanguageTools">Change the interface language? "Tools &gt; 語言 / Language" menu: 繁體中文, English, 日本語, 한국어; it takes effect at once and is remembered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_WantClaudeOrAnotherAI">Want Claude or another AI to help build models? Help menu → "Copy prompt for AI", paste it to the AI and replace the last line with what you want; the prompt tells the AI to read the manual (pstk.exe manual) first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_TheCommandLinePstkExe">The command-line pstk.exe sits next to PixelStacking.exe and opens no window; the .pstk files it makes can be opened directly in the editor. If a file the AI changed is also open in the editor, re-open it to see the changes (the editor does not reload automatically).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_Outline">Outline</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_OutlineSilhouette">Outer outline</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_OutlineSilhouette">Adds a line around the outside of the model, in a darker shade of the colour next to it. The line grows outside the model (exported images get one ring larger).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_OutlineCreases">Edge lines</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_OutlineCreases">Inside the model: draws a line, in a darker shade of the base colour, where faces of different orientation meet (top vs side…) and where something in front overlaps something behind. Stacked mode has no faces, so this does nothing there.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_OutlineWidth">Width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_OutlineWidth">Line width in pixels of the rendered image (the preview image or the exported image). For a large export scale pick a thicker line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_OutlineTone">Tone</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_OutlineLight">Light</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_OutlineMedium">Medium</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_OutlineDark">Dark</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_OutlineTone">Line colour = the base colour times this: light 70 %, medium 55 %, dark 35 %.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Common_ExportOutline">Outline (same settings as the preview)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Common_ExportOutlineHint">The outer outline takes pixels outside the model, so the image is one ring larger than without an outline. Line width, tone and which lines are drawn follow the preview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_OutlineDescription">Available in the preview and in PNG / GIF export: an outer outline (a ring around the model) and edge lines (where faces meet, and where something in front overlaps something behind), drawn in a darker shade of the base colour; width 1–3 and tone are adjustable. See "Outline" in the preview panel.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_EdgesHardToSee">Edges hard to see in the solid preview? Turn on "Outline" in the preview panel: the outer outline separates the model from the background and the edge lines make block corners clearer; tick "Outline" when exporting PNG / GIF to bake it in.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_Skirt">Skirt</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_FrontHair">Front hair (bangs)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_BackHair">Back hair</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_Ahoge">Ahoge (hair antenna)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_HairAccessory">Hair accessory</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_Cape">Cape</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_LeftEar">Left ear</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="PosePresets_RightEar">Right ear</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_CanvasZoom">Zoom</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_ZoomFit">Fit window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_CanvasZoom">Magnification of each cell on the edit canvas. "Fit window" stretches it to the largest size; with a fixed zoom, scroll with the scroll bars, the wheel or by dragging with the middle mouse button when it is larger than the window. You can also hold Ctrl over the canvas and scroll the wheel to zoom (centred on the cursor).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CanvasZoom">Canvas zoom: the "Zoom" menu at the top right fixes the size of each cell on the edit canvas (1×–64×). When it is larger than the window, move with the scroll bars, the wheel or by dragging with the middle mouse button; holding Ctrl and scrolling the wheel over the canvas also zooms (centred on the cursor). The default "Fit window" stretches it to the largest size.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_CanvasScroll">Scroll bars for the edit canvas (available once it is zoomed larger than the window). With the cursor over the canvas: wheel = scroll up/down, Shift + wheel = scroll sideways; dragging with the middle mouse button also pans.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help_CanvasScroll">Canvas scrolling: when zoomed beyond the window, drag the scroll bars at the right and bottom of the canvas. With the cursor over the canvas, the wheel scrolls up/down, Shift + wheel scrolls sideways and Ctrl + wheel zooms. Change layer with ←/→, [ ] or PageUp/PageDown instead.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_EditViewMarker">Edit view</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PreviewGizmo">The axes at the bottom left of the preview: red X, green Y, blue Z; the solid end points towards you and the faded end points away. The yellow circle is where the edit canvas on the left is looking from; the translucent yellow frame in the model is the layer being edited.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Opt_ShowEditLayerFrame">Show the edit-layer frame</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ShowEditLayerFrame">Marks the layer being edited on the left canvas with a dashed yellow frame inside the preview model. The frame is drawn over the image and is not hidden by voxels; untick it if it gets in the way. (The axes at the bottom left are not affected.)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Top">Top</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Bottom">Bottom</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Front">Front</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Back">Back</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Left">Left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Cube_Right">Right</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Lbl_PreviewViewButtons">Preview view</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_PresetViewButtons">Turns the preview to look from that side (and stops auto-rotate): Front = from +Y, Back = from −Y, Right = from +X, Left = from −X, Top = from above, Bottom = from below. These match the directions of the edit views on the left.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip_ViewCube">View cube: click a face to turn the preview to look from that side (this also stops auto-rotate). The cube turns with the preview; the face with the yellow border is the direction the edit canvas on the left is looking from.</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
